# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` in deploy/app.Dockerfile ships the host's
# node_modules into the build stage — hundreds of MB, slow, and on a Windows
# host full of binaries the Linux image cannot use. The build stage runs its own
# `npm ci` from the lockfile, which is the only node_modules that matters.

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
coverage
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Per-deployment secrets and config. The app image must not bake either one in:
# .env reaches the containers through compose's env_file, and
# viewpoint.config.ts is read by the serverless api/* functions, not by the
# static bundle.
.env
.env.local
.env.production
viewpoint.config.ts

# Python
capture-service/.venv
capture-service/venv
capture-service/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]

# Generated at install time, mounted at runtime — never baked into an image.
deploy/certs

# Tooling and test artefacts
.vercel
.partykit
.qwen-tasks
.qwen
test-results
playwright-report
e2e
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/__tests__
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log

# Large sample assets the Vite build does not import from the repo root.
Videos Post linkedin
